+      (ControlIntentBatch), discriminated by the NATS header key
+      `intent_encoding` — matched EXACT-CASE, byte-for-byte, because
+      nats.go headers are verbatim case-sensitive (no MIME
+      canonicalization): ABSENT ⇒ v2 (every pre-ADR-0026 producer; other
+      headers are ignored), `tsib` ⇒ TSIB, ANY OTHER VALUE (including
+      present-but-empty) ⇒ the message is dropped and counted
+      (intentEncodingUnknown), logged loudly — never a fall-through to v2
+      parsing, so a future encoding against an old engine fails loudly
+      instead of misparsing. A valid TSIB expands at ingest into
+      per-vehicle records in record order; everything downstream (claim
+      filter, per-controller seq, hold-last, arbitration, record plane)
+      is identical to the v2 stream.
+      Migration (ADR-0026 M4): deploy engine first, drivers second. A
+      pre-ADR-0026 engine has no demux rule: a multi-record TSIB payload
+      read as v2 fails v2 structural validation — dropped and counted as
+      malformed v2, never silently applied; the pathological
+      single-record case (68 B, bytes 40–41 reading as route_len 24) can
+      pass v2 decode and then dies at claim filtering — the named
