+    IntentEncodingHeaders:
+      type: object
+      required: [intent_encoding]
+      properties:
+        intent_encoding:
+          type: string
+          const: tsib
+          description: 'TSIB discriminator (ADR-0026). Matched EXACT-CASE, byte-for-byte — nats.go headers are verbatim case-sensitive, no MIME canonicalization. Absent key ⇒ the message is per-vehicle v2; any other value (including present-but-empty) ⇒ dropped and counted (intentEncodingUnknown), logged loudly.'
+
+    TSIBFrame:
+      type: string
+      format: binary
+      description: |
+        v1, little-endian (ADR-0026):
+          header (24 B): magic "TSIB" | version u16 = 1 | flags u16 (reserved, 0) |
+                         tick u64 | count u32 | reserved u32
+          records: count × 44 B — byte-identical layout to the fixed
+            section of IntentFrame (vehicle_id u64 | flags u32 |
+            lane_delta i32 | accel f64 | speed_setpoint f64 | signals u32 |
+            turn i32 | route_len u16 | reserved u16; flag semantics as
+            defined there).
+        Whole-batch structural validity — a violation drops the WHOLE
+        batch (counted intentBatchDropped, logged), never partially
+        applied: exact length 24 + 44·count; version 1; count ≤ 20000
+        (880,024 B with the header — under the 1 MiB per-message
+        discipline; larger fleets split into multiple batches per tick);
+        every record's route_len MUST be 0 AND flag bit4 (route present)
+        MUST be clear — a route update rides one complete standalone v2
+        intent for the tick and the vehicle is omitted from that tick's
+        batch. Per-record SEMANTIC checks are per-record as in v2: a
+        NaN/Inf accel or speed setpoint drops ONLY that record (counted
+        intentRecordDropped); the rest of the batch applies.
+        tick is INFORMATIONAL ONLY (the source observation tick, for
+        diagnostics and applied-lag measurement) — never validated and
+        never gating acceptance; ingest is arrival-based exactly as for
+        v2. The flags u16 and reserved u32 header fields are IGNORED on
+        decode: reserved bits are not must-understand — an extension that
+        requires understanding them needs a version bump.
+
+    TSIBView:
